        "original_id": "6961c517-8a8c-5f0c-9124-680bd3c7abb5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tamiami Canal, Genesee River, Flagami\n- Topics: Waterways, neighborhood boundaries\n\nFacts:\n- The Genesee River is a tributary of Lake Ontario that flows northward through the Twin Tiers of Pennsylvania and New York in the United States.\n- The Tamiami Canal flows west to east from the western part of Florida in the Everglades past Miami International Airport to a salinity control center near the Miami River.\n- Flagami is a neighborhood in Miami, Florida, defined roughly as south and east of the Tamiami Canal, north of the Tamiami Trail, and west of Red Road.\n- Flagami is bisected by Flagler Street.",
